/-! #2979's dispatch table (mdumitrean's allocation, `research/rank7-joint-endframes/allocation/DISPATCH.json` sha256 65e435bd68e97243c003677271b88485a29d4d0fae2dff1354100404a145e74c and
`ORDER.json` sha256 519d1d5dbb997a219fcfcad34c0b03e7838bef24199784d7e964fa10090f66e1 on main, read-only copies): 666 calls (74 replicas x 9 stages), provider 0 = `extra` (416 calls),
provider 1 = `gauge44` (250 calls).  `dispKB`: bit `k` = provider of call `k = 9 ρ + l`; `dispGB`: bit `τ` = provider of
the call at global time `τ` (bit tables: the kernel reads a bit in one step).  Generated by x-tables/tools/mk_disp2979.py (wht45/lever2979, 19 Oct 2026; p-disp's generator, instance #2979), which
checks the order (every call once, stages increasing in time per replica), the tags and the counts, and refuses a count
